<%
// Shared event month-grid, with month/year dropdowns and narrower Prev/
// Next arrows - a real request: "Parent portal events, events page
// should show the same event calendar that is on main admin portal."
// Main Admin (views/admin-events-list.ejs) and every member-facing
// portal (views/events-list.ejs, via routes/events.js) already build
// their calendar DATA from the exact same utils/events.js monthGrid() -
// this partial is the rendering they now share too, replacing the
// member-facing page's own older, simpler markup (plain Prev/Next text
// links, no month/year dropdowns) so the two never drift apart again.
//
// locals: calendar (monthGrid()'s own shape), monthLinkBase (a URL up
// through its own `view=X` query param, no `&month=` yet - e.g. Main
// Admin's "/main-admin/events?tab=calendar&view=calendar" vs. the
// shared "/events?view=calendar" - each caller's own routing, appended
// to below), eventHref(e) - one event pill's own link target (Main
// Admin's own builder page vs. the shared public event detail page).
//
// leadingViewToggle/trailingIcons (both optional, Student Portal only
// today - views/events-list.ejs) - a real request: "Student portal,
// events tab should say event calendar... Export, pdf and print icons
// should be in a single row, not column, side by side... Shrink to fit
// entire row together clean on mobile." A corrected follow-up to an
// earlier "desktop only, Export/PDF/Print after Next, view toggle on its
// own row above the grid" design (desktopTrailingIcons/
// desktopTopRightToggle, now gone) - the Prev/Month/Year/Next/Export/
// Print/PDF controls are ONE row, at every width. A later real request
// ("Calendar vs list view icons should be on the 3rd row by themselves")
// moved the List/Calendar toggle - briefly folded into that same row -
// back out onto its own row underneath instead (the same plain
// .class-schedule-view-toggle pair every other List/Grid toggle in the
// app already uses, not the cramped icon-shrinking this row's own
// mixed-width controls need). leadingViewToggle is {view,
// portalQuerySuffix}; trailingIcons is an array of {href, icon, label,
// target?}. The nav row carries no .roster-btn-row (styles.css's own
// unscoped mobile rule turns any .roster-btn-row into an evenly-columned
// CSS grid sized for a handful of equal buttons, not 7 mixed-width
// controls that need to shrink down to icon-size while the month/year
// selects stay legible) - .event-calendar-nav-row-unified is its own
// flex row with its own shrink rules instead. %>
<div class="event-calendar-toolbar no-print">
  <% if (typeof leadingViewToggle !== 'undefined' && leadingViewToggle) { %>
    <div class="event-calendar-nav-row event-calendar-nav-row-unified">
      <a class="roster-action-btn event-calendar-nav-btn" data-nav-dir="prev" href="<%= monthLinkBase %>&month=<%= calendar.prevParam %>">&larr; Prev</a>
      <select id="event-month-select" class="event-month-select" onchange="window.location.href='<%- monthLinkBase %>&month='+document.getElementById('event-year-select').value+'-'+this.value;">
        <% for (let m = 1; m <= 12; m++) { %>
          <option value="<%= String(m).padStart(2, '0') %>" <%= calendar.month === m ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= new Date(Date.UTC(2000, m - 1, 1)).toLocaleString('en-US', { month: 'long', timeZone: 'UTC' }) %></option>
        <% } %>
      </select>
      <select id="event-year-select" class="event-year-select" onchange="window.location.href='<%- monthLinkBase %>&month='+this.value+'-'+document.getElementById('event-month-select').value;">
        <% for (let y = calendar.year - 3; y <= calendar.year + 3; y++) { %>
          <option value="<%= y %>" <%= calendar.year === y ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= y %></option>
        <% } %>
      </select>
      <a class="roster-action-btn event-calendar-nav-btn" data-nav-dir="next" href="<%= monthLinkBase %>&month=<%= calendar.nextParam %>">Next &rarr;</a>
      <% if (typeof trailingIcons !== 'undefined' && trailingIcons) { %>
        <% trailingIcons.forEach(function(b) { %>
          <a class="icon-btn event-calendar-nav-trailing-icon" href="<%= b.href %>"<% if (b.target) { %> target="<%= b.target %>"<% } %> aria-label="<%= b.label %>" title="<%= b.label %>"><svg class="icon"><use href="#<%= b.icon %>"/></svg></a>
        <% }); %>
      <% } %>
    </div>
    <%# A real request: "Calendar vs list view icons should be on the 3rd
        row by themselves" - its own row, after the registration-buttons
        row (events-list.ejs) and this Prev/Month/Year/Next/Export/Print/
        PDF row, not folded into either - the same plain .class-schedule-
        view-toggle pair every other List/Grid toggle in the app already
        uses, no special shrinking needed now that it's not sharing a row
        with 7 other mixed-width controls. %>
    <div class="class-schedule-view-toggle" role="group" aria-label="List or calendar view">
      <a class="icon-btn<%= leadingViewToggle.view === 'list' ? ' icon-btn-active' : '' %>" href="/events?view=list<%= leadingViewToggle.portalQuerySuffix %>" aria-pressed="<%= leadingViewToggle.view === 'list' %>" aria-label="List view" title="List view"><svg class="icon"><use href="#icon-clipboard-list"/></svg></a>
      <a class="icon-btn<%= leadingViewToggle.view === 'calendar' ? ' icon-btn-active' : '' %>" href="/events?view=calendar<%= leadingViewToggle.portalQuerySuffix %>" aria-pressed="<%= leadingViewToggle.view === 'calendar' %>" aria-label="Calendar view" title="Calendar view"><svg class="icon"><use href="#icon-calendar-check"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  <% } else { %>
    <%# A real request: "mobile view. the row should be small left arrow,
        month drop down, year drop down, small right arrow. all in one
        row neatly," later: "the arrow buttons should be half the size" -
        see public/js/roster-btn-row-grid.js's own data-fixed-column-widths
        escape hatch (its default grid only counts .roster-action-btn
        children, never the two <select>s below, so left to its own
        default it split these 4 controls into two rows instead of one). %>
    <div class="roster-btn-row event-calendar-nav-row" data-fixed-column-widths="1fr 2fr 2fr 1fr">
      <a class="roster-action-btn event-calendar-nav-btn" data-nav-dir="prev" href="<%= monthLinkBase %>&month=<%= calendar.prevParam %>">&larr; Prev</a>
      <select id="event-month-select" class="event-month-select" onchange="window.location.href='<%- monthLinkBase %>&month='+document.getElementById('event-year-select').value+'-'+this.value;">
        <% for (let m = 1; m <= 12; m++) { %>
          <option value="<%= String(m).padStart(2, '0') %>" <%= calendar.month === m ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= new Date(Date.UTC(2000, m - 1, 1)).toLocaleString('en-US', { month: 'long', timeZone: 'UTC' }) %></option>
        <% } %>
      </select>
      <select id="event-year-select" class="event-year-select" onchange="window.location.href='<%- monthLinkBase %>&month='+this.value+'-'+document.getElementById('event-month-select').value;">
        <% for (let y = calendar.year - 3; y <= calendar.year + 3; y++) { %>
          <option value="<%= y %>" <%= calendar.year === y ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= y %></option>
        <% } %>
      </select>
      <a class="roster-action-btn event-calendar-nav-btn" data-nav-dir="next" href="<%= monthLinkBase %>&month=<%= calendar.nextParam %>">Next &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  <% } %>
</div>

<% if (calendar.weeks.every(function(w) { return w.every(function(d) { return !d.inMonth || d.events.length === 0; }); })) { %>
  <p class="roster-empty">No published events this month.</p>
<% } %>
<div class="roster-scroll">
  <table class="roster-table condensed-table event-calendar-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Sun</th><th>Mon</th><th>Tue</th><th>Wed</th><th>Thu</th><th>Fri</th><th>Sat</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% calendar.weeks.forEach(function(week) { %>
        <tr>
          <%# A real request: "The dates on the calendar view should only
              be October dates. If viewing November it should only show
              November dates. Currently it shows a few of the dates from
              the previous month and upcoming dates for the next month."
              monthGrid (utils/events.js) still pads the grid with
              adjacent-month days so every week is a real 7-day row and
              the weekday columns line up - that part is unchanged - but
              a leading/trailing cell (day.inMonth === false) now renders
              as a plain blank cell instead of showing the other month's
              own date number (and, incidentally, its events - an event
              on Oct 31 no longer shows twice, once on October's own
              grid and once padding November's). %>
          <% week.forEach(function(day) { %>
            <% if (!day.inMonth) { %>
              <td></td>
            <% } else { %>
              <td>
                <div><%= day.day %></div>
                <% day.events.forEach(function(e) { %>
                  <a href="<%= eventHref(e) %>" class="badge-pill<%= e.status === 'cancelled' ? ' event-title-cancelled' : '' %>" style="<%= e.categoryColor ? `background:${e.categoryColor};color:#fff;` : '' %> display:block; margin-top:2px;"><%= e.title %><% if (e.status === 'cancelled') { %> CANCELED<% } %></a>
                <% }); %>
              </td>
            <% } %>
          <% }); %>
        </tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
